## 5. Architecture

**Frontend:** Mobile-first PWA. React + TypeScript + Vite (or Next.js). Tailwind or CSS variables with design tokens. Framer Motion (or Motion One) for animation. Installable manifest. Works at 360–430px wide first, then scales to tablet/desktop with a centered device frame.

**Widget:** Build the same app also as an embeddable bundle:
- `<script src=".../looksmith.js" data-key="..." data-theme="..."></script>` injects launcher button and a full-screen iframe/sheet.
- Communicates with host via `postMessage`: `looksmith:ready`, `looksmith:add-to-bag {sku[]}`, `looksmith:close`.
- Include `demo-store.html`: a fictional retailer page embedding the widget.

**Backend:** Node (Express/Fastify) or Python (FastAPI). Responsibilities:
- `/api/skin` `/api/tone` `/api/tryon/cloth` `/api/tryon/makeup` — thin typed proxies over YouCam with caching, retries, polling.
- `/api/agent/plan` `/api/agent/critique` `/api/agent/explain` — Gemini calls.
- `/api/catalog` — serves catalog adapter output.
- `/api/share-card` — optional server-side card render (or do client canvas).
- Streaming progress to client via SSE for the Agent Stage.
- Config via `.env`; ship `.env.example`.

**AI model:** Gemini **3.5 Flash Lite** via Google GenAI SDK.
- Model id from env `GEMINI_MODEL` (default to the Flash Lite id available in the SDK; verify exact string in Google AI docs and record it).
- Use **structured JSON output** with schema validation (zod/pydantic). Temperature ≤0.4.
- Roles: (a) Planner, (b) Critic (may use multimodal input of the try-on result), (c) Copywriter for one-line rationales.
- **Fallback:** deterministic rules-based planner if Gemini errors or times out. App must never dead-end.

**Catalog adapter:** Normalise any retailer feed to:
```ts
type Product = {
  sku: string; title: string; brand: string; price: number; currency: string;
  category: 'top'|'bottom'|'dress'|'outerwear'|'ethnic'|'shoes'|'bag'|'accessory'|'jewellery';
  colorName: string; colorHex: string; imageUrl: string; // clean flat-lay or cutout
  tags: string[]; occasion: string[]; url: string; inStock: boolean;
};
```
Ship `seed/catalog.json` with 40–60 products across fictional brands (§9). Images: generate or use license-free/own images. No trademarked logos.

**Storage:** No user photo persistence by default. In-memory/session only. Optional "Save looks" stores result thumbnails locally (IndexedDB) with explicit consent. "Delete my data" button must work.

