## 7. Design System — "Quiet Luxury, Human First"

**Design brief in one line:** a calm, editorial, confidence-building experience. Feels like a personal stylist, not a filter app. Every pixel intentional.

### 7.1 Principles
1. **Calm over loud.** Generous whitespace. One focal point per screen.
2. **The user is the hero.** Their face/look is always the largest element. UI recedes.
3. **Honest waiting.** Never a dead spinner. Show progress, meaning, and what is happening.
4. **Gentle language.** Skin talk is kind, never clinical or shaming. No red "bad" scores. Use "areas to care for", not "problems".
5. **Direct manipulation.** Drag, swipe, press, hold. Things respond under the finger.
6. **Consistency.** 4pt grid. Same radii, same motion, same tone everywhere.
7. **Accessible by default.** WCAG AA contrast, 44×44pt targets, screen-reader labels, reduced-motion support.

### 7.2 Design tokens (CSS variables; retailer can override a subset)
```
/* Colour — neutral base */
--canvas:        #FAF8F5;   /* warm off-white */
--surface:       #FFFFFF;
--surface-2:     #F3EFE9;
--ink:           #14110F;
--ink-2:         #5B554E;
--ink-3:         #8F887F;
--hairline:      rgba(20,17,15,0.08);
--danger:        #B3261E;   /* errors only */
--success:       #2E7D5B;

/* Dynamic accent — set AFTER tone analysis from user's palette, fallback brand */
--accent:        #1F3A34;
--accent-soft:   color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, white);
--on-accent:     #FFFFFF;

/* Dark mode: canvas #0F0E0D, surface #1A1816, ink #F4F1EC; keep accent contrast ≥ 4.5:1 */

/* Type */
--font-display:  "Instrument Serif", "Cormorant Garamond", Georgia, serif;
--font-ui:       "Inter", -apple-system, "SF Pro Text", system-ui, sans-serif;
Scale (px/line): Display 40/44 · Title 28/34 · Headline 20/26 · Body 16/24 · Callout 14/20 · Caption 12/16
Weights: display 400, UI 400/500/600. Tight tracking on display (-0.01em). Tabular numerals for prices/scores.

/* Space (4pt): 4 8 12 16 20 24 32 40 56 72 */
/* Radius: chips 999 · buttons 14 · cards 24 · sheets 28 · images 20 */
/* Elevation: e1 0 1px 2px rgba(20,17,15,.06) · e2 0 8px 24px rgba(20,17,15,.08) · e3 0 24px 60px rgba(20,17,15,.14) */
```
Retailer-overridable: `--accent`, `--font-display`, `--radius-scale`, logo slot, launcher style. Nothing else.

**Dynamic accent:** after Tone Analysis, derive an accent from the user's palette (pick the most flattering deep swatch with AA contrast against `--on-accent`). The whole UI subtly tints with a 480ms crossfade. This is the signature moment: "the app became yours."

### 7.3 Motion language
- Easing standard: `cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1)`. Springs for direct manipulation: stiffness 300, damping 30, mass 1.
- Durations: micro 120ms · small 200ms · medium 320ms · large 480ms · hero 640ms.
- Stagger lists by 40–60ms, max 8 items.
- Transitions are **spatial**: shared-element hero image from card → detail; sheets rise from bottom with rubber-banding; back swipe edge gesture.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`: replace movement with 120ms fades. Never lose information.
- Haptics: `navigator.vibrate` short pulses (10–15ms) on success/commit where supported. Graceful no-op elsewhere.
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Target 60fps on a mid-range Android.

### 7.4 Micro-interaction catalogue (build all, each precisely)
**Capture**
- Face guide: soft oval. Idle = thin 1.5px hairline. When face is centred, lit, and sharp → ring thickens to 3px and fills with accent via a 320ms stroke animation + light haptic. Live hints in plain words: "Move a little closer", "Find softer light", "Hold still".
- Shutter: press scales to 0.94, release springs back; flash overlay 80ms; captured image shrinks into a thumbnail at the corner with a spring.
- Retake/Use buttons: magnetic hover on desktop, press-down depth on touch.

**Scan & Profile**
- Scanning: a soft light band sweeps over the face (1.4s ease-in-out, loop) with subtle vignette. Copy cycles: "Reading your skin tone…", "Looking at texture…", "Finding your palette…".
- Result reveal: concern overlays fade in staggered (60ms) as gentle dots/blooms over the photo; tap a chip → matching region pulses once and others dim to 40%.
- Scores count up with tabular numerals (600ms ease-out). No red. Use a calm single-hue ramp.
- Palette swatches pop in like drops (scale 0.6→1 spring, 50ms stagger). Long-press a swatch → shows name ("Warm Sand") and copy hex.
- Accent takeover crossfade (see 7.2).

**Occasion input**
- Chips with spring select (scale 1.04 → 1), check morph. Free-text field grows smoothly; placeholder rotates examples every 3s.
- Budget slider: thumb enlarges while dragging; live value bubble above thumb; snaps softly at nice numbers; haptic ticks.

**Agent Stage (hero moment — spend design effort here)**
- Vertical timeline of agent steps streamed via SSE. Each step: icon → morphs to animated check (stroke draw, 240ms) when done.
- Steps in human language: "Choosing colours from your palette", "Trying on the olive linen shirt", "Checking skin comfort for your makeup", "Swapped the red scarf — it clashed with your undertone".
- The swap/self-correction step gets emphasis: strikethrough old item → slide in new item (shared-element), subtle accent underline.
- Live thumbnails of looks "develop" like film: blurred monochrome → colour sharpen over 640ms as each VTO returns.
- Never show raw JSON, model names, or jargon. A discreet "Details" disclosure shows technical trace for judges (YouCam tool + Gemini role per step).

**Look Carousel**
- Horizontal paged cards with peek of next card. Rubber-band at ends. Parallax: image moves 8% slower than card on drag.
- Subtle gyro/pointer tilt (max 3°) on the hero image; disabled for reduced motion.
- Before/after: press-and-hold image to peek original; or drag a handle with magnetic snap at 0/50/100%.
- Skin-safe badge: shield icon draws in (stroke 400ms) on card appear. Tap → bottom sheet explaining why in kind language.
- Item chips under image: tap → item sheet with swap alternatives (3 options, each previewed with a mini try-on thumbnail when affordable; otherwise flat-lay).
- Swap: old item chip lifts and fades; new chip slides into place; hero image shows a soft shimmer sweep while VTO re-renders, then crossfades (320ms).
- Like: heart bloom (scale 1→1.25→1 + 6 tiny particles), then a "Learning" chip floats up and docks in header. Dislike: soft shrink + gentle fade of card with Undo toast (5s).
- Intensity slider for makeup: live label ("Soft ↔ Bold"); releasing triggers re-render with progress ring on the slider thumb.

**Bag**
- Add to bag: item thumbnails arc along a curved path into the bag icon (480ms); icon bounces once; count morphs (odometer roll).
- Bag sheet: swipe-to-remove with undo; price total animates numerically; "Checkout on {Retailer}" primary button full width, press depth.

**Share Look Card**
- Card renders as a poster: user's look, name of look, palette dots, skin-safe badge, retailer logo slot, small "Styled with LOOKSMITH". No raw face-analysis scores on card by default (privacy toggle to include).
- Hold-to-share: circular progress around button fills over 600ms then fires native share; fallback download PNG.
- Preview tilts with device motion; subtle foil shimmer on palette dots.

**System states**
- Skeletons match final layout (shimmer 1.6s, low contrast).
- Image load: blur-up (LQIP) → sharp crossfade 320ms.
- Errors: friendly, specific, one clear action. Example: "That photo was a bit dark. Try near a window." + [Retake].
- Offline/slow: persistent unobtrusive banner; queue actions where sensible.
- Empty states have illustration + one action.
- Toasts: bottom, 3s, swipe to dismiss, never cover primary CTA.

### 7.5 Layout & components
- Safe-area aware (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`). Sticky bottom action bar with blur (backdrop-filter) and hairline top border.
- Primary button: 52px height, full width on mobile, accent fill, on-accent text, 14px radius. Secondary: surface-2 fill. Tertiary: text only.
- Bottom sheets with grabber, snap points (peek/half/full), drag-to-dismiss with velocity.
- Typography hierarchy: serif display for emotional moments (headlines, look names); UI sans for everything functional.
- Iconography: single family, 1.5px stroke, rounded caps (e.g., Lucide). Custom-draw only the shield badge and logo mark.
- Imagery: photos with soft 20px radius, no heavy borders, subtle inner shadow `inset 0 0 0 1px var(--hairline)`.

### 7.6 Copy & tone
Warm, brief, respectful. Short sentences. No exclamation spam. No beauty-shaming. No medical language. Examples:
- Consent: "Your photo is used only to style you. It isn't stored unless you save a look."
- Profile: "Here's what we noticed. This is a cosmetic read, not medical advice."
- Skin-safe: "Chosen to feel gentle on skin that runs a little sensitive."

### 7.7 Accessibility checklist
- Contrast AA in light and dark. Visible focus rings (2px accent, 2px offset).
- All interactive elements labelled; images have meaningful `alt` (look descriptions).
- Dynamic type: layout survives 130% text scale.
- Animations have reduced-motion equivalents. No flashing >3Hz.
- Don't rely on colour alone to convey state.
- Camera permission denied → clear fallback: upload from gallery.

### 7.8 Responsive behaviour
- ≤430px: native-app feel, bottom nav/action bar.
- 431–1024px: centered 430px app column over soft background.
- ≥1025px: split view for judges: app on left in phone frame; right side shows optional "Under the hood" panel (agent trace + API calls + unit counter). Toggle-able, off in widget.

